<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26786" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διηνεκής</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διᾱνεκής</span></b>  (v. infr.) <i><span class="en">
			<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
			1.327.10
		</span></i> (Callatis, <span class="entity">i A. D.</span>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>continuous, unbroken,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτραπιτοί τε διηνεκέες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					13.195
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νώτοισι . . διηνεκέεσσι</span>
			with slices <i>cut the whole length</i> of the chine, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				7.321
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥίζαι, ῥάβδοι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				12.134
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				297
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ ὦλκα διηνεκέα προταμοίμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					18.375
				</span></i>
			; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. σώματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Hp.Ma.</u>
					301b
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Anaxandr.
				6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				646.22
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρος δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					3.1.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κανών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					7.3073.108
				</span></i>
			 (Lebad., <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ δ.</span>”
				<i>regularity,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					2.355
				</span></i>
			; of Time, <i>perpetual,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. νυκτί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>VH</u>
					1.19
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δικτάτωρ εἰς τὸ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					App.
					<u>BC</u>
					1.4
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διηνεκέως</span> in phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἀγορεύειν</span> to tell <i>from beginning
				to end,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				7.241
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				12.56
			</span></i> (<i>distinctly, positively,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				4.836
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅπαντα δ. κατέλεξε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					627
				</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἕκαστα διηνεκὲς ἐξενέποντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.391
				</span></i>
			; 
				Boeot.
			 and 
				Dor.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διανεκῶς</span>
			<i>without ceasing,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὕδειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Corinn.
					9
				</span></i>
			 (dub.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				793.3
			</span></i> (Cos, <span class="entity">i A. D.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διηνεκῶς</span> once in Trag., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				319
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
				382
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				2.17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				194.12
			</span></i> (Egypt, <span class="entity">i B. C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				D.Chr.
				49.8
			</span></i>, etc.; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διηνεκές</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Ap.</u>
					255
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				158
			</span></i>; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὸ διηνεκές</span> in
				<i>perpetuity,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ep.Hebr.
				7.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PRyl.</u>
				2.427
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>JHS</u>
				33.338
			</span></i> (Macedonia, <span class="entity">ii A. D.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>
			<i>invariably,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλεονάκις,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18(2).315
			</span></i>.—The 
				Aeol.
			 and 
				Dor.
			 form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διᾱνεκής</span> is used
			also in 
				Att.
			, as <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Hp.Ma.</u>
				301b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				301e
			</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				Diogenian.
			</span></i> ap. Sch. ad loc.), <i><span class="en">
				Anaxandr.
			</span></i> l. c., <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				2.1054.81
			</span></i>; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόμος διηνεκής</span> a
				<i>perpetual</i> law is read in <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				839a
			</span></i>.</div>
